\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: East Europe/Brazil -3: Matches Losses In W. Europe \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 14:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although falling in response to Franco's resignation, emerging stock markets haven't been suffering to any greater degree than their Western European counterparts. While Germany's benchmark Dax index was down 6.2% midday, Turkey's IMKB-100 index was down 4.1% at 2558.60. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the lira. Such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are routine, however, although the lira did fall by more than its average daily depreciation of between 0.12% and 0.15%. Against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basked composed of $1 and EUR0.77, the lira is down 0.2%, with the dollar at TRL329,900, up from Tuesday's close at TRL322,550. \par \par \uc2  The Israeli shekel was down against the dollar, which was trading around ILS4.0730, a loss of some 0.4% since the Bank of Israel's fixing of ILS4.0580 to the dollar Tuesday. The TA-100 Index of the shares with the heaviest market capitalization was down 2.2%. \par \par \uc2  Around 1305 GMT, the Johannesburg Stock Exchange's composite All Share Index was down 244.6 points, or 4.2%, at 5618.40 - considerably shaving gains from the first week of January. \par \par \uc2  The rand was trading at ZAR6.1500 to the dollar, compared with ZAR6.0200 in late trade Tuesday. Dealers said the rand is vulnerable to further bad news from Brazil. \par \par \uc2  "I would put a solid floor on the rand at ZAR6.0000, but think it could easily fall to ZAR6.2500-ZAR6.3000" against the dollar, said Luke Shearer, director of offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Standard Bank Investment Corp. \par \par \uc2  -Paul Hannon; 44-171-832 9513; paul.hannon@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1332GMT \par \par \uc2  1192 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1d00a0a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
