\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira steady vs dlr after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1998\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Nov 26 (Reuters) - Dollar sales re-emerged in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank on Friday due to a mounting liquidity squeeze caused by tax payments, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold lira for dollars towards the close to guard its daily lira depreciation target, after buying lira for dollars on Thursday. The bank had also sold lira for dollars on Tuesday and Wednesday this week. \par \par \uc2  Banks' best bids and offers ended at around 302,500 and 302,800 lira to the dollar, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Cash demand strengthened as the money market opened 524.4 trillion lira short on Friday due to banks' value-added tax payments, estimated at around 150 trillion lira. \par \par \uc2  "There were also minor dollar sales from abroad. The lira's daily depreciation rate fell to around 0.12 percent as dollar sales accelerated towards the close," one banker said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the lira's daily depreciation rate up to 0.15 percent at the close, the banker added. \par \par \uc2  Bankers say this figure is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily depreciation target for November, estimating its monthly target at 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  They expect the liquidity squeeze to continue with private sector salary payments next week. \par \par \uc2  But they add that mild dollar demand may emerge due to foreigners' dollar purchases after their holdings of Turkish treasury papers mature next Wednesday when the treasury will service 625 trillion lira of domestic debt. \par \par \uc2  Political developments over the weekend are also expected to play a major role in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade next week. \par \par \uc2  Turkish President Suleyman Demirel is holding talks with party leaders in the search for a coalition to replace the minority government of Prime Minister Mesut Yilmaz, who was toppled because of corruption allegations eralier this week, but is staying on in a caretaker capacity. ((Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 0875, fax +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubr03fdf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
