\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira ends easier vs dlr on higher parity. \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1998\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira eased to around 296,600 versus the dollar on Thursday from a previous close of 295,300, due to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the mark abroad, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold lira for dollars towards the close on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank in a second straight day. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mild and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in to guard its daily lira depreciation target in the face of banks' dollar sales at the close," said one banker. \par \par \uc2  "My estimate is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases on Wednesday and Thursday is not more than $200 million," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bankers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target rate for daily lira depreciation for November stands at around 0.15 percent, which produces a monthly lira depreciation of 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said dollar sales were fuelled mainly by the liquidity shortage which worsened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent strong \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy lira for dollars last week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dived $1.166 billion to $20.277 billion in the week ending on November 13, due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy lira for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Bankers expect political uncertainty to block banks' dollar sales next week when the fragile three-party government coalition is likely to be toppled by a censure vote called by the opposition. \par \par \uc2  The censure motion debate began in parliament at 1300 GMT. ((Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 0875, fax +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubj045ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
