\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sparked By Banks' Dollar Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1998\par 14:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Dollar-selling by commercial banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday afternoon, with the bank selling Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the lira's depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the commercial banks' dollar-selling was driven by the need to meet lira demand. In general, dollar selling demand in the market indicates relative calm and high lira rates. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the dollar closed at TRL296,500, up from Tuesday's close of TRL295,450. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained a monthly lira depreciation rate of 4.4% against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay +90 212 512 5017; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1329GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubj01aml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
