\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Aims To Suppress Dollar Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 09:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early Friday and bought lira (TRL) for dollars, aiming to suppress dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started when bank bids were at TRL278,350 or higher. \par \par \uc2  At about 0718 GMT, dollar bids were at TRL278,230, down from 278,550 at 0600 GMT and from late Thursday's TRL279,600. \par \par \uc2  The bank is seen as maintaining a daily 0.01% depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Before the market opened at 0700 GMT, the daily depreciation rate was at about 0.02%. \par \par \uc2  Traders said more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; 90 312 512 5017; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0738GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8s07bcc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
