\par\par \b \uc2  Wrap: Turkey's Markets Decline Sharply; No End In Sight \b0\par\par\uc2  By Selim Atalay \par \uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 19:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Turkey was pulled down into the vortex that consumed emerging markets throughout the planet Thursday, and market participants are pessimistic on the propsects for stability being restored soon. \par \par \uc2  "Can it get worse? Yes it can," said Mehmet Akkent, a director at Istanbul's Ata Securities. "There's no upside potential," he said. \par \par \uc2  That was certainly true Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The main Istanbul Stock Exchange IMKB-100 index closed the day with a 13.1% tumble, at 2603.99 points, down 393.26 points from Wednesday's 2997.25 points. \par \par \uc2  The annual compounding rate on benchmark government bonds touched 130%, up from Wednesday's 120%. \par \par \uc2  And the dollar closed at 278,680 Turkish lira (TRL), up from Wednesday's TRL278,350, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's descent. \par \par \uc2  As was the case almost everywhere else in emerging markets Thursday, local and foreign investors left in bulk, participants said, driven by concerns the situation in Russia could repeat itself in other venues. \par \par \uc2  Looking forward, both the continuing international volatility and domestic factors are likely to result in further declines. Fiscal problems require stable government policy, but hopes for this are fading with elections scheduled for April 1999. \par \par \uc2  But all isn't bleak, according to some. "Markets are declining, but for the short term Turkey has minimal foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk," said Cem Akyurek, an economist at Istanbul's Global Securities. He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by raising rates and selling dollars is firmly controlling the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the lira's daily depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark basket at 0.01% Thursday, with a \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1742GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07bqe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
