\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  On Dollar Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 14:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Turkish lira (TRL) for dollars Friday afternoon after bearish sentiment on emerging markets was felt in the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said dollar demand by a European bank ten minutes before the market closed fueled overall dollar buying demand, inviting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors, nervous about the situation in Russia and Venezuela, are seen having switched from lira to dollars. \par \par \uc2  Friday afternoon, the Istanbul Stock Exchange main index was down 6.2% and traders suspect those sellers might also demand dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came when commercial bank dollar bids were at TRL276,750. \par \par \uc2  At the market's 1200 GMT close, bids were lower at TRL276,600, but still above Thursday's close of TRL276,060. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank maintained the daily 0.09% lira depreciation against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 312 512 5017; satalay@ap.org. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1241GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8l075h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
