\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -3: Another  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 11:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said commercial banks are selling dollars for their lira needs. \par \par \uc2  Primarily, the new 6.6% tax on repo transactions and 13.2% tax on interbank lira deposit transactions, which were activated Thursday, have unnerved the bond market due to rising costs, and consequently the prices are falling. \par \par \uc2  On the lira interbank market, the overnight rate reflects the high lira demand, as the rate averages 72.64%. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the lira had been appreciating against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket since early on. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only brought the daily lira depreciation down to zero and after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exit, the lira started appreciating again. \par \par \uc2  Traders see another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  With Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing for Friday, the lira's July depreciation was 2.41% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  At about 0909 GMT, the bank dollar offers were at TRL270,720, up from Thursday's close of TRL269,750. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At about 0909 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DEM1.7810, from DEM1.7793\par around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and DEM1.7805 late Thursday in New York.\par    -By Selim Atalay +90 312 512 5017; satalay@ap.org.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 3