\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish cenbank drains cash after  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1998\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1345 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained 29.2 trillion lira at 41 percent on onvernight money deals when a cash squeeze eased after its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell lira for dollars before the market closed. \par \par \uc2  * Average overnight money rate fell to 45.43 percent from previous 63.42 percent after a brushing a high of 73 percent on pension salaries and tax payments in the morning. \par \par \uc2  * Overnight repo ended firmer at 65.94 on tax-free deals and at 70.30 percent on taxed deals compared to the previous close of 46.41 and 49.38 percent, respectively. \par \par \uc2  * Bond yields went up by around three percentage points to 78 percent levels on firmer funding costs and emerging talks over an early poll. \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, July 21 (Reuters) - A Turkish money market cash squeeze which stemmed from petroleum consumption tax payments and pension salaries eased in the afternoon due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell lira for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The bank drained 29.2 trillion lira at 41 percent on overnight deals at close of the market. The average overnight money rate ended at 45.43 percent, down from Monday's 63.42 percent after touching 73 percent during the day. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling lira for the dollar as daily lira depreciation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced below of daily limits on markets' severe demand for the lira," said one banker. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the bank raised the lira's daily depreciation level to 0.1 percent after the intervetion. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily depreciation target is estimated at around 0.08 percent for July after June's 0.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  Higher cost of funding in line with a cash squeeze earlier in the day caused bond yields to rise around three percentage points to around 78 percent levels. \par \par \uc2  The most active papers were March 10 and April 14 yielding 78.12 and 77.96 percent, up from previous 75.16 for both. \par \par \uc2  "Bond yields returned from 80 percent which is seen as offering technical resistance in the day. In line with firmer funding cost and uncertainty about early poll talks, the yields may keep rising tendency in coming days," said one banker. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said renewed political concerns after coalition leaders' statements on early elections also upset the market. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Mesut YIlmaz, under pressure from coalition partners to announce a date for early general elections, said on Tuesday parliament would decide in October when to hold the polls. \par \par \uc2  He told a meeting of his Motherland Party that he would call for a summer parliamentary recess from next week to October, adding that the long-awaited tax reform would pass this week. \par \par \uc2  Overnight repo rates, the indication cost of bond funding, remained above of the previous yields by around 20-21 percentage points at 65.94 percent on tax-free deals and 70.30 percent on taxed deals. \par \par \uc2  ((Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 0875 fax, +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7l00eix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
