\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Overnight-3: Slow Depreciation Hints At  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 10:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Turkish lira (TRL) is lower against the dollar in midday trading Monday in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's three-days depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is 0.33%, slower than current inflation trend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen keeping the lira's depreciation in line with the inflation rate. \par \par \uc2  Around 0752 GMT, dollar bids at the interbank market were at TRL258,520, up from Friday's close at TRL257,000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements were at TRL258,800, with dollar rate at DEM1.7760, up from Friday's close at TRL257,640 and DEM1.7720. \par \par \uc2  At 0752 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DEM1.7762, up slightly  from DEM1.7760 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and DEM1.7750 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Tulin Oguducu, a dealer at Istanbul's Bank Express, said persistent dollar selling by some commercial banks on Monday, amid a slow lira depreciation rate, might cause the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling lira to maintain its depreciation rate target. \par \par \uc2  -By Mike Zemene; +90 312 466 3101 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0815GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6804tvx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
