\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -3: Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Russia Effect \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1998\par 15:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heavy and aimed at both slowing the lira's depreciation and meeting the dollar demand of commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  At the market's 1200 GMT close, commercial bank dollar bids were at TRL254,270, up from Friday's TRL252,250. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate was at TRL254,250, up from Friday's TRL252,930. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the daily lira depreciation rate to 0.11%, from a high of 0.16%. The current monthly depreciation rate is at 3.6%. Traders last week were looking at a monthly depreciation rate of 3.2%, but they believe the bank can further lower the depreciation rate in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  As for other markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Tuesday due to a national holiday. Traders said the break may settle local markets. \par \par \uc2  Monday's volatility was seen as a direct result of declining Russia markets, and foreign funds were retreating from East European emerging markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign banks based in Turkey were also among Monday's heavy dollar buyers. \par \par \uc2  The volatility also hurt the bond market and the Feb. 17, 1999 paper auctioned Monday for an annual rate of 93.51% was quoted at 94.72% in the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  -By Selim Atalay; +90 212 512 5017; satalay@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones