\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira eases vs dollar despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, April 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira eased to 247,500 to the dollar on Monday from Friday's 246,150, with the lira's daily devaluation afected by high inflation and a higher dollar/mark parity, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in late trade by buying lira for dollars to meet banks' growing dollar demand in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The lira had weakened to 247,650 to the dollar before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  just before the interbank market closed. \par \par \uc2  "Banks' daily hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs dominate foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank at the close. There was again demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to square their dollar deposits," said a banker. \par \par \uc2  "The bank lowered the daily lira devaluation rate to 0.13 percent from 0.15 percent by buying lira for dollars just before the close," said one banker. \par \par \uc2  Mild demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerged in the morning due to a rising cash surplus and a higher dollar/mark parity in international markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained 80.3 trillion lira of a 110.8 trillion surplus by holding a 79-day reverse repo auction. \par \par \uc2  The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last sold lira for dollars on Friday to raise the daily lira depreciation rate to 0.13 percent from 0.03 amid dollar sales by banks to raise cash. \par \par \uc2  "As long as monthly inflation rate does not dip under 4.0 percent, I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will target a monthly devaluation below that," said another banker. \par \par \uc2  The lira shed 4.8 percent of its value against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in March when wholesale inflation was 4.0 percent. ((Mete Akcok, Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 0875, fax +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4k071kf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
