\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish lira eases vs dollar after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL, March 25 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira ended easier at 240,200 per dollar on Wednesday, versus Tuesday's 239,600 on two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the daily cost of funding related to \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's high inflation, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the bank sold lira for dollars both in the morning and afternoon sessions to raise the lira's daily depreciation to its target rate, in the face of continued selling pressure on hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a severe liquidity shortage. \par \par \uc2  "The lira's devaluation rate remained under 0.1 percent all day. After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it went up to 0.15 percent," a banker said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said high interest rates on repos also began to divert cash away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market ahead of a long public holiday in early April. Turkish markets will close for a 4-1/2-day Islamic holiday from noon on April 6. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira devaluation target at around five percent against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket this month, parallel to expectations of lower March inflation. \par \par \uc2  The lira lost 5.5 percent of its value against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in February when wholesale inflation was 4.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key dollar rate for banks' compulsory \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transfers was the best bid in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for most of the day. The key dollar rate closed at 239,860 lira, up from 239,290 on Tuesday. ((Mete Akcok, Istanbul newsroom, +90-212-275 0875, fax +90-212-267 2137, istanbul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3p08nd4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
