\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Lira Down Against Dollar;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Watch On \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1998\par 11:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira (TRL) is lower against the dollar in midday trading Tuesday in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's daily depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is 0.15%. Dealers said the market is very calm due to the Ramadan holiday that starts officially on Wednesday afternoon, but added that there is some dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  Around 0943 GMT, dollar bids at the interbank market were at TRL214,970, up from Monday's close at TRL214,330. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements were at TRL215,010, with dollar rate at DEM1.7863 from Monday's close at TRL214,350 and DEM1.7800. \par \par \uc2  At 0943 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DEM1.7855, compared with DEM1.7859 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo but lower than DEM1.7960 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Funda Celik, a dealer at Istanbul's Chase Manhattan, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon to sell lira for dollars, if the lira's current low daily deprecation rate persists. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen keeping a monthly lira depreciation rate of 4.58%-4.65%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened a ten-day repo auction and sold\par TRL183.1 trillion at an average 80.5% interest rate to provide some\par liquidity to the lira-tight market. The market opened TRL159.2 trillion\par short.\par -By Mike Zemene; +90 312 466 3101\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1016GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1r00pqm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
