\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 /Bank -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Raise Lira Depreciation \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey sold lira (TRL) for dollars in the morning trading Thursday to raise the lira's depreciation rate and to add to its foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the lira depreciation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket to 0.16%, corresponding to a monthly 4.79%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Around 1007 GMT, dollar bids at the interbank market were at TRL214,400, from Wednesday's close at TRL215,290. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements was TRL214,500, with dollar rate at DEM1.8087 from Wednesday's close at TRL215,450 and DEM1.8328. \par \par \uc2  At 1007 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DEM1.8082, compared with DEM1.8005 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and DEM1.8195 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Until the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders noted, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the best\par bidder. Dollar selling by commercial banks for lira lowers the lira\par depreciation. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb lira depreciation\par beyond its targets.\par -By Selim Atalay; +90 212 512 5017; satalay@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-98\par \f28 \