\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Lira Down Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1997\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is lower against the dollar midday Monday with some dollar buying demand. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's three day depreciation rate since Friday against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is a relatively high 0.65%. \par \par \uc2  A trader said the monthly lira depreciation rate corresponds to 5.40% and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might prefer to lower it to 5.2% by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buying lira for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT, dollar bids at the interbank market were at 204,570 lira, up from the previous close at 203,550 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements was at 204,430 lira, with the dollar rate at DM1.7743 from the previous close at 203,420 lira and DM1.7727. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DM1.7737, compared with DM1.7710 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and DM1.7735 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there is dollar buying demand as banks and companies minimize their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure for the year-end balance sheets. Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen to control the lira's depreciation rate through market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar buying continues despite an overall lira demand, as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened a seven day repo auction Monday and sold 131.3\par trillion lira with an average rate of 83.45%. The market opened 313.5\par trillion lira short.\par -By Mike Zemene; +90 312 466 3101\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0945GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtct09yn7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
