\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Down Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Watch On \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is lower against the dollar midday trading Monday in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate. \par \par \uc2  The market is mixed with some dollar buying and selling. Traders said the lira's three-day depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is 0.58%. \par \par \uc2  Around 1010 GMT, dollar bids at the dollar/lira interbank market were at 200,100 lira, up from Friday's close at 198,600 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements were at 199,970 lira with dollar parity at DM1.7742 from Friday's close at 198,580 lira and DM1.7667. \par \par \uc2  At 1010 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DM1.7748 compared with DM1.7802 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and DM1.7760 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Bulent Yagli a trader at Istanbul-based Interbank said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon to lower the lira's depreciation speed. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in December, selling dollars, to lower the daily depreciation speed to around 0.16% from 0.20%. \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  enable banks to buy dollars at a cheaper rate and also meets existing dollar buying demand. There is a general dollar buying demand due to year-end balance sheet considerations and government preparations to launch a capital gains tax. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market did not show any reaction to Finance Minister Zekeriya Temizel's statement over the weekend that the plan to tax capital gains might be postponed to 1998. \par \par \uc2  The government's tax plan has created a strong dollar buying demand and caused a tension in capital markets. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, despite dollar buying demand there is also a lira shortage\par in the market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened a seven-day repo auction on\par Monday and sold 128 trillion lira at 83.2% average interest rate, to\par provide some liquidity to the lira-tight market. The market opened 324.4\par trillion lira short.\par -By Mike Zemene; +90 312 466 3101\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1105GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcf09lsg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
