\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Afternoon  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1997\par 15:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought lira for dollars in afternoon trading Tuesday following a round of morning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders had been expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon session amid dollar buying demand from some banks which pulled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the lira. \par \par \uc2  The bank's afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range started when the lira's daily depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche Mark basket was at 0.19% with 199,060 lira to the dollar. At the market's close, daily lira depreciation rate was at about 0.13% and with 198,900 lira to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key dollar buying rate closed at 198,800 lira with dollar rate at DM1.7887. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues keeping a tight lira depreciation rate against the dollar to ensure market stability. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1424GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc909gec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
