\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Anticipated \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 14:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought lira for dollars Tuesday afternoon in a heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in an effort to reduce the lira's daily depreciation rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders had anticipated the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the lira's monthly depreciation rate against the dollar/DM basket had risen to 5.95%. After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rate slowed down to its usual 5.75%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started when commercial banks' dollar bids were at 189,100 lira and above. At the time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key dollar buying rate was 188,940 lira. \par \par \uc2  At the 1200 GMT market close, banks' bids were at 188,770 lira and lower from midday Tuesday's 188,960 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key dollar-buying rate was at 188,690 lira, with the dollar rate at DM1.7277. \par \par \uc2  Traders say dollar demand continues at tolerable levels and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping a firm hand on the market. \par \par \uc2  An Istanbul-based trader said the daily depreciation rate was pushed higher by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at intraday trading. Arda Turerer, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Istanbul's Ottoman Bank said banks aren't rushing to buy dollars to cover their short positions, but some might be opting to close positions for year-end accounting purposes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the market showed no reaction to reported comments by state\par minister responsible for the Treasury Gunes Taner that Turkey will enter\par a 'unique' deal with the International Monetary Fund.\par By Selim Atalay  +90 312 4663101\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1358GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbi08t6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
