\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Dn Against Dlr; Traders Expect  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par 10:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ANKARA (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is lower against the dollar in midday trading Tuesday in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira's daily depreciation rate against the dollar/Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is 0.4% for the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there is strong dollar buying demand in the foreign market and added that \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon to trim the high daily devaluation rate. \par \par \uc2  Around 0938 GMT, dollar bids at the dollar/lira interbank market were at 188,960 lira, up from Monday's close at 188,890 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements were at 188,940 lira, with dollar parity at DM1.7286 from Monday's close at 188,890 lira and DM1.7398. \par \par \uc2  At 0938 GMT, the dollar was quoted at DM1.7257 from DM1.7293 around 0545 GMT in Tokyo and DM1.7310 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ayse Tagma a trader at ABN Amro Bank in Istanbul said the State\par Minister responsible for the Treasury Gunes Taner's statement that\par Turkey will sign an agreement with the International Monetary Fund is\par not expected to have an immediate impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par -By Mike Zemene; +90 312 466 3101\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2