\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Down Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Watch On \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 11:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is trading lower against the dollar early Tuesday in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key dollar buying rate. \par \par \uc2  Traders said last week's tense dollar buying demand by foreign investors is partly over, but foreign buying revived during Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting latent demand at a lower dollar rate. Some traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again buy lira for dollars Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0931 GMT, dollar bids at the dollar/lira interbank market were at 183,470 lira, from Monday's close at 183,730 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' 14% minimum reserve requirements was at 183,450 lira with dollar parity at DM1.7290. Monday's close was at 183,700 lira with dollar parity at DM1.7410. \par \par \uc2  Around 0931 GMT, the dollar is quoted at DM1.7280, compared with DM1.7305 around 0525 GMT in Tokyo and DM1.7365 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, equally strong lira demand is squeezing the lira market as the interbank market opened Tuesday 220 trillion lira short. At normal times, traders said, commercial banks would sell their dollars for lira, but the market is uneasy and the dollar demand is from investors who are leaving bond and stock portfolios after last week's global correction. \par \par \uc2  Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market faced a false alarm Tuesday morning as an international wire service reported that Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying lira for dollars. The report caused a brief panic but was denied by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1009GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb408eax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
