\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's Lira Slightly Up Vs Dollar With Dlr's Cross Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1997\par 09:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is slightly higher against the dollar Tuesday in line with dollar's cross rates moves, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The market eyes Tuesday's T-bond auction by the Turkish Treasury and waits for the release of March inflation data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  A trader said there might be a small-scale dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday if commercial banks' dollar bids are too jumpy. \par \par \uc2  Around 0750 GMT, dollar bids at the dollar/lira interbank market were at 127,460 lira, down from Monday's close at 127,650 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' minimum reserve requirements were at 127,300 lira, down from Monday's close at 127,550 lira. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT, the dollar is at 1.6715 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.6750 marks late Monday in New York and below 1.6789 marks in London Monday. It is also at 123.55 yen, below 123.75 yen late Monday in New York and down from 123.94 yen late Monday in London. \par \par \uc2  The Turkish Treasury Tuesday is holding a two-year Consumer Price Index (CPI)-indexed bond auction and participants expect an uneventful sale of around 30 to 40 trillion lira. \par \par \uc2  A sale below the level will be a surprise and can move the dollar buying bids higher, they added. \par \par \uc2  The lira's March depreciation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of one dollar and 1.5 marks is seen at 4.7% and the market's average inflation expectation is 5.3%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0758GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4102a0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
