\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Lira Stable Vs Dlr; Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 1997\par 14:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira closed stable against the dollar Wednesday following incognito dollar sales that came minutes before the market's close. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they suspect it was the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  that made the sales and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market once again. The bank has been selling dollars since last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said about 10 minutes before the market's 1300 GMT close, offers at 120,880 lira for a dollar were posted at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controlled trading screens. \par \par \uc2  They added that this could be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the going offers at the interbank market were higher. Traders believe only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can afford to sell below the going market rates. \par \par \uc2  At 1300 GMT, the dollar bids at the dollar/lira interbank market were at 120,890 lira, down from Tuesday's close at 121,050 lira to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 1200 GMT, the dollar was 1.6934 Deutsche marks , up from 1.6852 marks in Tokyo at 0530 GMT and 1.6850 marks ate in New York Tuesday. It was 123.88 yen, flat with 123.90 yen and 123.88 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the latest incognito \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be an extension of the bank's policy to make its presence felt in the market. \par \par \uc2  'The bank likes to inject fear to the market,' said an Istanbul trader. 'The bank wants to emphasize that it can control the dollar rate.' \par \par \uc2  Traders said there has been a dollar buying demand since last week, partly fueled by the dollar's international gains. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen to aim a 4% monthly lira depreciation against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of 1 dollar and 1.5 marks. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1337GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2j015xu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
