\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Politics -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Seen Breaking Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 19:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen aiming at a 4% monthly basket depreciation rate for the month of February. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures the lira's depreciation against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, comprised of 1 dollar and 1.5 Deutsche marks. \par \par \uc2  'With \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar buying demand should be broken at some point,' said Uruz Ersozoglu, senior vice president at Osmanli Bankasi in Istanbul. 'We, the bankers, aren't worried much about the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the interest rates.' \par \par \uc2  Participants said political tension is also partly to blame for the recent climb of the annual compounding rates of treasury bills to 95% from the 80% of early January. \par \par \uc2  'For a target annual inflation rate of 70% to 75%, the t-bill rate of 95% is normal,' Ersozoglu said. \par \par \uc2  Kanijali of Citibank added that with banks' continuing t-bill needs for their repurchase-agreement positions and reserve requirements, even papers above 95% will find buyers and this will curb the dollar buying demand. \par \par \uc2  Some participants also note that with high lira overnight lending rates, at 70% and above, banks are unlikely to keep up dollar buying demand. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar buying demand slows when the overnight rate closes to 70%,' said Murat Argun, senior dealer at WestLB (Europa) AG's Istanbul Branch. 'For the alarm bells, one still needs to watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. But no one knows exactly how much of the reserves are usable.' \par \par \uc2  Participants believe the dollar buying demand can be broken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but only after forceful selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They note, however, that if the dollar's gains at international markets continue, so will the dollar buying demand. The catch point is that while investors buy dollars with hopes of further gains, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is less annoyed with the dollar's individual gains as it watches its dollar/mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. \par \par \uc2  Participants added that for the lira's immediate future, they need to see the February inflation data scheduled for release March 4. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1849GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2h01200\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
