\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 /Bank -3: Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  At Next-Day's Quotes \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 11:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unexpected as the market was trading on next day settlement quotes because of the Presidents Day in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  But they added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was related with the bank's seven-day repurchase securities agreements auction that aimed to draw part of the 44.5 trillion lira of excess cash in the market. The bank drew 25.3 trillion lira with an average rate of 67.1% and immediately after the results, banks' dollar bids rose by 50 lira to 120,950 lira. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT close of the morning trading session, the dollar bids at the interbank market were at 120,740 lira, up from Friday's 119,940 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey posted a dollar buying rate of 120,450 lira for Tuesday, up from intraday Friday's 119,700 lira. \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 1.6927 Deutsche marks, compared with 1.6928 marks around 0545 GMT in Tokyo and 1.6875 marks late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that in its fourth daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aiming to keep a 4% monthly depreciation rate for the lira against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of 1 dollar and 1.5 marks. At the time of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the depreciation rate was 4.5%, said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Overall, the market is watching Tuesday's parliament votes which will be a test for coalition government's lifespan. Also, there are increasing rumors that Moody's Investors Service will further downgrade Turkey's rate of Ba3 long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign ceiling for bonds. \par \par \uc2  Although the market is aware of the Moody's negative attitude since January and believes that the government will last, uneasiness reflects itself as a dollar buying demand, traders added. The demand is also fueled by small investors who follow the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent gains from the popular press and buy hoping that it will rise further. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1023GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2h00zu5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
