\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Closes Lower Vs Dlr Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1997\par 19:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira closed lower against the dollar Wednesday despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars for the lira. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank aims to keep the lira's depreciation rate under its control and added that more dollar selling by the bank might come Thursday if the market pushes for higher rates than the bank's target. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets a lira depreciation of 4% against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in February. The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket consists of 1 dollar and 1.5 Deutsche marks. At time time of Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the depreciation was over 4.2%, traders added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank sold dollars about 10 minutes before the market's 1300 GMT close. The dollar/lira rates were at 119,800 lira at the time of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and were rolled down to 119,450 lira at the market's close. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the market to open Thursday morning at a dollar rate of 119,750 lira. \par \par \uc2  An Istanbul bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't severe as when the dollar selling started, banks were fast to lower their rates by 100 lira at each round. \par \par \uc2  'If banks were worried, the rates would decrease by 10 lira at each round, not by 100,' he added. 'Banks weren't keen on buying dollars.' \par \par \uc2  In order not to loose reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes before the trading session closes, traders believe. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1856GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2c015uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
