\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Sold Dlrs At 105,330 Lira \b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1996\par 14:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the second time Monday, selling dollars minutes before the market closed, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said that in the afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars starting at 105,330 lira and gradually falling to about 105,300 lira. At the market close at 1300 GMT, the dollar was at 105,280 lira. \par \par \uc2  'The bank keeps a daily lira depreciation rate of 0.2% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket' of 1 dollar and 1.5 Deutsche marks, a trader said, adding that the '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't very aggressive.' \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day sold dollars at a rate beginning at 105,400 lira and gradually falling to 105,330 lira. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1334GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscg01q13\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
