\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Lira Down Vs Dollar; Banks Expecting  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1996\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is trading lower against the dollar early Monday in a nervous market following the sovereign rate downgrading by the Standard & Poor's. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the lira is weaker than Friday, but up from its early Monday lows after banks sold dollars in anticipation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There was no excessive dollar buying demand at the market or a lira selling from abroad, but bankers said man-on-the-street might start a buying demand. \par \par \uc2  'Relative calm is due to the expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell dollars,' said an Istanbul trader. 'If not, then we'll see the dollar going up the roof.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT the dollar bids at the interbank market were at 105,340 lira, up from Friday's 104,270 lira. Early Monday, market bids were at 105,500 lira, but came down when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a dollar buying rate of 105,000 lira and shortly raised its rate to 105,050 lira. \par \par \uc2  Around 0855 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 1.5551 marks, compared with 1.5545 marks earlier in Asia and 1.5545 marks late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar's climb in international markets will relieve the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it won't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell dollars to curb the rate increase. \par \par \uc2  But they added that from Friday, the lira's depreciation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of 1 dollar and 1.5 Deutsche mark was at 0.60% and is higher than the regular 0.48% to 0.52%. \par \par \uc2  S&P lowered its long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on the Republic of Turkey to single-B from single-B-plus and has affirmed its single-B short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-12-96 \par \par \uc2  0952GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscg01pbm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
