\par\par \b \uc2  Turkey Shares Close Down 0.75% On Decreased Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1996\par 17:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--Turkish shares closed 0.75% lower Tuesday following a slowdown in traders' speculation, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said recent record index climbs were led by selective trading of major speculators who were hoping others would follow. But now the speculators' activity has slowed down, leading to a declining index, they added. \par \par \uc2  The main Istanbul Stock Exchange IMKB-100 index closed at 93,217.11 points, down 700 points or 0.75% from Monday's 93,917.28 points. Trading volume was at 14 trillion lira, up from Monday's 12 trillion. \par \par \uc2  Tan Egeli of Interbank AS attributed Tuesday's decline to the dollar's recent gains against the lira. \par \par \uc2  'There was a capital outflow today,' said Egeli. 'Currently capital in the market is speculative. If dollar goes up any further, this capital can leave the market for the dollar.' \par \par \uc2  During this time of year, the dollar rate has been known to increase. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday by selling dollars to bring the dollar rate down  to 104,020 lira from 104,380 lira. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers don't see a speculative rise in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kamelya Isler of Eczacibasi Securities in Istanbul said other markets don't offer an alternative to the stock market. 'We have no competition,' she said, adding that a correction might take the index down to 90,000 points, but only to be followed by another increase. \par \par \uc2  Some of the active shares Tuesday were included Yapi Kredi bank, closing at 2,800 lira, up 100 lira or 4%; Intema marketing, rising to 3,750 lira, up 150 lira or 4%; Medya Holding, increasing to 1,225 lira, up 25 lira or 2%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1613GMT \par \par \uc2  5070 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsca01o3s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
